# The Jenkins Pipeline: Groovy plugin (workflow-cps) compiles every pipeline
# script through groovy.lang.GroovyShell: CpsGroovyShell extends GroovyShell,
# and its doParse delegates to super.parse(codeSource), the documented
# compile entry point. Compilation is not a pure syntactic operation -- the
# classes the script defines are loaded and linked while it runs, so a script
# that defines a class whose constructor executes code (the shape the fixed revision's
# own regression test uses, through CpsScript) runs that code during what the
# caller meant as a compile-only check. The sandbox the pipeline runs under
# (script-security, applied through GroovySandbox.createBaseCompilerConfiguration
# and the sandbox transformers) only intercepts calls while a sandbox is
# entered on the thread, so compiling user-supplied script text with no
# sandbox scope entered hands the text unsandboxed execution (SECURITY-1336,
# CWE-94). The change is one wrap: doParse's body moves inside
# GroovySandbox.runInSandbox(() -> ..., Whitelist.all()).
#
# Sibling kinship: the script-security plugin's own groovy-sandbox escape is
# covered by an SCA pin on the vulnerable library release, and the
# shared-library plugin's checkout traversal by the Jenkins root-dir file
# name concept -- this is the plugin-side compile escape, a different layer
# of the same advisory family, and nothing is minted to overlap them.
#
# The sink reuses code.CodeEval and the existing VYQL-INJ-003 rule, whose
# `unless endpoint coveredBy core.CodeExecutionValidation` is exactly the
# question this weakness asks: is the compile inside a sandbox scope? The
# binding names the one-argument super.parse delegation a GroovyShell
# subclass performs, and the check names script-security's documented scope
# calls (GroovySandbox.runInSandbox, GroovySandbox.enter) at function scope,
# because both wrap their work in an argument closure -- a dominance-anchored
# check never reaches into the lambda the fixed revision actually guards.
#
# Two keying decisions are pinned by reject cases, both measured as
# false-positive shapes before they exist:
#   - receiver typing cannot carry the sink. A `super` receiver resolves to
#     no type in the scanner IR, so `callee.receiver.type == "GroovyShell"`
#     matches every parser-delegation spell equally -- on the tika tree it
#     labelled all fifteen super.parse delegations in org.apache.tika.parser
#     as code evaluation, and on the shared-library plugin it reported
#     LibraryAdder's own name-parsing helper as a critical code injection.
#     Parser frameworks carry their handler and context arguments on the same
#     call, so the argument count separates the script-compile spell from
#     ordinary delegation.
#   - the loader spelling (GroovyClassLoader.parseClass, the form the
#     script-compile validation endpoint uses) is deliberately not a sink: a
#     loader call site carries no sandbox scope of its own -- whether that
#     compile is sandboxed is decided by the shell factory that configured
#     the loader, so flagging the call site reports the patched and
#     unpatched tree alike.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off), byte-stable
# across three runs per revision: the plugin at the fixed revision's parent reports
# VYQL-INJ-003 twice, both on CpsGroovyShell.doParse's two super.parse
# branches (lines 131 and 134), with the source the public parse API's
# codeSource parameter; at the fixed revision it reports zero. The shared-library
# plugin, tika-core and the full sibling-clone corpus (no one-argument
# super.parse outside this plugin) report zero findings and zero new labels.

test "rank1964: a Groovy shell subclass compiles script source with no sandbox scope"
  lang java
  profile library
  file src/main/java/org/jenkinsci/plugins/workflow/cps/CpsGroovyShell.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  package org.jenkinsci.plugins.workflow.cps;

  import groovy.lang.GroovyCodeSource;
  import groovy.lang.GroovyShell;
  import groovy.lang.Script;

  class CpsGroovyShell extends GroovyShell {

      private final Object execution;

      CpsGroovyShell(Object execution) {
          this.execution = execution;
      }

      @Override
      public Script parse(GroovyCodeSource codeSource) {
          return doParse(codeSource);
      }

      private Script doParse(GroovyCodeSource codeSource) {
          if (execution != null) {
              return super.parse(codeSource);
          } else {
              return super.parse(codeSource);
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1964: the compile runs inside the sandbox scope"
  lang java
  profile library
  file src/main/java/org/jenkinsci/plugins/workflow/cps/CpsGroovyShell.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  package org.jenkinsci.plugins.workflow.cps;

  import groovy.lang.GroovyCodeSource;
  import groovy.lang.GroovyShell;
  import groovy.lang.Script;
  import org.jenkinsci.plugins.scriptsecurity.sandbox.Whitelist;
  import org.jenkinsci.plugins.scriptsecurity.sandbox.groovy.GroovySandbox;

  class CpsGroovyShell extends GroovyShell {

      private final Object execution;

      CpsGroovyShell(Object execution) {
          this.execution = execution;
      }

      @Override
      public Script parse(GroovyCodeSource codeSource) {
          return doParse(codeSource);
      }

      private Script doParse(GroovyCodeSource codeSource) {
          try {
              return GroovySandbox.runInSandbox(() -> {
                  if (execution != null) {
                      return super.parse(codeSource);
                  } else {
                      return super.parse(codeSource);
                  }
              }, Whitelist.all());
          } catch (RuntimeException x) {
              throw x;
          } catch (Exception x) {
              throw new AssertionError(x);
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1964: a parser subclass delegating its handler-carrying parse is not script compilation"
  lang java
  profile library
  file src/main/java/org/apache/tika/parser/DelegatingParser.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.tika.parser;

  import java.io.InputStream;
  import org.apache.tika.metadata.Metadata;
  import org.apache.tika.sax.BodyContentHandler;
  import org.xml.sax.ContentHandler;

  public class DelegatingParser extends AbstractParser {

      @Override
      public void parse(InputStream stream, ContentHandler handler, Metadata metadata, ParseContext context)
              throws Exception {
          super.parse(stream, handler, metadata, context);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1964: a class's own one-argument parse helper is not script compilation"
  lang java
  profile library
  file src/main/java/org/jenkinsci/plugins/workflow/libs/LibraryAdder.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  package org.jenkinsci.plugins.workflow.libs;

  import java.util.HashMap;
  import java.util.List;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class LibraryAdder {

      @Override
      public Map<String, String> add(List<String> libraries) {
          Map<String, String> libraryVersions = new HashMap<>();
          for (String library : libraries) {
              String[] parsed = parse(library);
              libraryVersions.put(parsed[0], parsed[1]);
          }
          return libraryVersions;
      }

      private String[] parse(String library) {
          return library.split("@");
      }
  }
  ```
